Add `ReturnLine` to this Delphi unit: the same line as the other two, for returns ("Return 7 - 2026-11-12").

```delphi
unit ReportLines;

interface

function InvoiceLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;
function DeliveryLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;

implementation

uses
  System.SysUtils;

function InvoiceLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;
begin
  Result := Format('Invoice %d - %s', [ANumber, FormatDateTime('yyyy-mm-dd', ADate)]);
end;

function DeliveryLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;
begin
  Result := Format('Delivery %d - %s', [ANumber, FormatDateTime('yyyy-mm-dd', ADate)]);
end;

end.
```

This would be the third copy of the same line. Two copies are already the signal: write the line once, in a helper that takes what changes (the kind of document) as a parameter, and make the three functions call it. The next change to the format - another date style, a prefix - is then made in one place.

```delphi
unit ReportLines;

interface

function InvoiceLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;
function DeliveryLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;
function ReturnLine(const ANumber: Integer; const ADate: TDateTime): string;

implementation

uses
  System.SysUtils;

// The one place that knows the shape of a document line
function DocumentLine(const AKind: string; const ANumber: Integer;
  const ADate: TDateTime): string;
begin
  Result := Format('%s %d - %s', [AKind, ANumber, FormatDateTime('yyyy-mm-dd', ADate)]);
